Group F of the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] consisted of [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]], [[Bosnia and Herzegovina national football team|Bosnia and Herzegovina]], [[Iran national football team|Iran]] and [[Nigeria national football team|Nigeria]]. Play began on 15 June and ended on 25 June 2014. The top two teams, Argentina and Nigeria, advanced to the round of 16.

