==Matches==
===Argentina vs Bosnia and Herzegovina===
The two teams had met in two previous matches, both in friendlies, most recently in 2013, both won by Argentina.<ref>{{cite web|title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=18 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |page=18 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140629232249/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf |archivedate=29 June 2014 }}</ref>

Bosnia and Herzegovina conceded three minutes into their World Cup debut, when [[Lionel Messi]]'s free kick from the left was flicked on by [[Marcos Rojo]] and bounced off [[Sead Kolašinac]] into the net for an own goal. In the second half, Messi played a one-two with substitute [[Gonzalo Higuaín]] and shot home from the edge of the penalty area with his left foot into the bottom-right corner.<ref>{{cite news |first=Jonathan |last=Wilson |title=Lionel Messi's sparkle returns to secure Argentina victory over Bosnia |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/16/argentina-bosnia-herzegovina-world-cup-group-f-match-report |work=The Guardian |publisher=Guardian News and Media |date=16 June 2014 |accessdate=30 October 2014 }}</ref> With five minutes remaining in normal time, Bosnia and Herzegovina pulled one back, when [[Senad Lulić]]'s pass found substitute [[Vedad Ibišević]] to score the country's first ever World Cup goal, shooting under the goalkeeper with his left foot.<ref>{{cite web |first=Mandeep |last=Sanghera |title=World Cup: Argentina 2-1 Bosnia-Hercegovina |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285099 |publisher=BBC Sport |date=15 June 2014 }}</ref>

Kolašinac's own goal after two minutes and nine seconds broke the record for the fastest [[own goal]] in the history of the FIFA World Cup, surpassing [[Carlos Gamarra]]'s own goal (two minutes and 46 seconds) in [[Paraguay national football team|Paraguay's]] [[2006 FIFA World Cup Group B#England vs Paraguay|first group stage match]] against [[England national football team|England]] at the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]].<ref>{{cite news |first=Mike |last=Janela |title=World Cup records fall in Brazil as tournament reaches the quarterfinals |url=http://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/news/2014/7/notable-records-broken-at-the-world-cup-after-the-round-of-16-58497 |publisher=Guinness World Records |date=2 July 2014 |accessdate=28 December 2014 }}</ref>

